Ours (dsv41 recipe), Apache-2.0, against vLLM main 6e517b15 + patches 0001-0015.
A hook for out-of-tree MoE quant methods that run a decode step's whole MoE phase themselves. DeepseekV4MoE (V4 and
V4.1) asks its routed experts' quant method for `fused_moe_forward(moe, hidden_states, input_ids)` before calling the
FusedMoE runner; a tensor return is the layer's output (already TP-reduced), None runs the runner as before. Without
such a method, or with it returning None, nothing changes. vllm_exl3_moe implements it with VLLM_EXL3_MOE_FUSED=1:
router GEMV + DeepSeek-V4 top-k + routed experts + the shared expert in one persistent exl3_smoe launch (Program P
stage P2), bit-identical to its router_topk + smoe(shared) pair (plugin tests/test_smoe_fused_gpu.py). V4.1's model is
not torch.compiled (no support_torch_compile), so the Python branch runs eagerly and inside FULL CUDA-graph capture.

diff --git a/vllm/models/deepseek_v4/nvidia/model.py b/vllm/models/deepseek_v4/nvidia/model.py
index a004120..90e9c04 100644
--- a/vllm/models/deepseek_v4/nvidia/model.py
+++ b/vllm/models/deepseek_v4/nvidia/model.py
@@ -1112,6 +1112,16 @@ class DeepseekV4MoE(nn.Module):
         self, hidden_states: torch.Tensor, input_ids: torch.Tensor | None = None
     ) -> torch.Tensor:
         org_shape = hidden_states.shape
+        # An out-of-tree quant method may run the whole MoE phase of a decode
+        # step itself (router, top-k, routed and shared experts, TP reduce),
+        # e.g. vllm_exl3_moe's one-launch exl3_smoe path; None keeps the runner.
+        fused = getattr(
+            self.experts.routed_experts.quant_method, "fused_moe_forward", None
+        )
+        if fused is not None:
+            out = fused(self, hidden_states, input_ids)
+            if out is not None:
+                return out.view(org_shape)
         final_hidden_states = self.experts(
             hidden_states=hidden_states,
             router_logits=hidden_states,
